# Nauss instances with 90 or 100 tasks and 25 or 30 machines (as in Pessoa et al. 2020), with ub = optimum + 1.
# Larger instances are in nauss-hard.batch. To solve an instance without a known upper bound, see the options
# -t (tentative upper bounds, as in nauss-tentative.batch) and -d (diving heuristic).
# Tip: after a batch execution, call 'grep statistics: out/nauss.out -h | cut -c13-' to get the results as rows for a LaTeX table.
# julia src/run.jl -b nauss.batch &> out/nauss.out
